<%# The live copy of this file is too large for the backup a sync takes
    before it changes live (SiteSync::BackupPolicy), so if the choice here
    replaces or deletes it on live, there's no copy to go back to. Said
    here, before the choice, rather than discovered afterwards.

    Only live's copy is at stake: picking "Keep live" or "Keep" for a file
    that's still on live leaves it alone. Video web versions are never
    backed up and are made again from the original, so they aren't named. %>
<% peer_size = conflict.dig("peer", "size") %>
<% if SiteSync::BackupPolicy.too_large_for_live_backup?(peer_size) && !SiteSync::BackupPolicy.video_web_version?(conflict["path"]) %>
  <p class="text-[11px] text-amber-800 mt-0.5">
    Live's copy (<%= number_to_human_size(peer_size) %>) is too large to back up before syncing.
    If you want to keep it, download it from the live site's Media Browser first.
  </p>
<% end %>
